%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 79c1856cac5ce614280ef9d32b707814, type: 3}
  m_Name: Sophia_recipe_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TeaRecipe
  introText: "Hi\u2026 I'm Sophia. I don't usually come to places like this, but
    I had to get out of my dorm for a bit."
  questionSets:
  - exchanges:
    - playerQuestion: "You\u2019re a student, huh? Did you come here to study or
        to take a break?"
      npcResponse: " I\u2026 Don\u2019t think about any of those. When I try to study,
        I can\u2019t tell if I\u2019m learning or if the words I repeat in my head
        just become background noise. And when I try to take breaks\u2026 I don\u2019t
        know\u2026 I keep thinking about needing to study."
    - playerQuestion: "You look tired\u2026 Hard time with the exams?"
      npcResponse: "Yeah, you could say that. It\u2019s as if it doesn\u2019t have
        an end. There are days when I wake up and feel as if I already lost time
        even if I didn\u2019t even start studying. I keep thinking about what will
        be on the exam paper, what if it\u2019s something I can\u2019t remember or
        didn\u2019t get to study altogether because I feel I don\u2019t have time
        to study everything properly."
    - playerQuestion: You seem to need something warm and a good conversation.
      npcResponse: " I think it would help\u2026 Maybe, at this point I\u2019m willing
        to try anything. It\u2019s as if my mind can\u2019t stay focused on one single
        task. Even when I\u2019m doing something else completely like eating or just
        walking my thoughts keep going astray."
  - exchanges:
    - playerQuestion: Do you think more about what could happen than what you are
        doing now?
      npcResponse: " That\u2019s the weird part, it\u2019s as if the present doesn\u2019t
        have any weight. What goes on, what could happen, what if\u2026 It doesn't
        stop to just one conclusion, it always keeps growing and I forget where I
        started from."
    - playerQuestion: "It\u2019s only for this exam or is it always like that?"
      npcResponse: "Mostly it\u2019s always like that because\u2026 Well it isn\u2019t
        necessarily about the exam, but what could happen before it even begins.
        The exam is already over in my mind, but many times no outcome I can think
        about is good enough."
    - playerQuestion: What is it that you think about so hard?
      npcResponse: "It\u2019s hard to explain, it\u2019s not only one thing. I think
        about studying, about my exam, how I would get there and what if something
        happens. I forget something or maybe I lose my bus."
  - exchanges:
    - playerQuestion: "When you finally stop studying or thinking about it\u2026
        what happens in your head?"
      npcResponse: "I thought stopping would feel like relief\u2026 but it doesn\u2019t
        really work like that. It\u2019s more like everything I tried to keep under
        control finally speaks at once. Not loudly, not aggressively\u2026 just constantly.
        Like small thoughts tapping on the same surface over and over again, reminding
        me they were there the whole time. Even when I\u2019m not doing anything,
        it doesn\u2019t stop."
    - playerQuestion: If you could remove one thing from all this pressure, what
        would it be?
      npcResponse: " I think\u2026 the part where my mind keeps jumping ahead of
        me. If I could just stay in one place mentally, even for a little while,
        everything would feel more manageable. But it keeps pulling me forward, like
        I\u2019m already late for something that hasn\u2019t even started yet. And
        I can\u2019t tell if I\u2019m preparing or just\u2026 exhausting myself before
        anything even happens."
    - playerQuestion: What scares you the most about not being ready?
      npcResponse: "I think it\u2019s more the idea that I\u2019ll realize too late
        that I didn\u2019t do enough. That I\u2019ll sit there and know the answer
        was somewhere in my head, but I just can\u2019t reach it anymore. And then
        everything I kept pushing myself for just collapsed into that one moment.
        That thought stays longer than everything else."
  requiredIngredients:
  - apa, sange
